          "source_text": "Functor of points.\nFor any <MATH_0001> there is a contravariant\nfunctor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich takes an object <MATH_0003> to the set\n<MATH_0004>. In other words <MATH_0005> is a presheaf.\nGiven a morphism <MATH_0006> the corresponding map\n<MATH_0007>\ntakes <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>. We will always denote\nthis presheaf <MATH_0010>.\nIt is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> associated to <MATH_0011>.\nIf <MATH_0012> is the category of schemes this functor is\nsometimes referred to as the\n<EMPHOPEN_0001>functor of points<EMPHCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0013>.\n",
